===Etymology===
From {{compound|en|water|line}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{rfp|en}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-waterline.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Flame, not lame-waterline.wav|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|nautical}} A line formed by the [[surface]] of the [[water]] on the [[hull]] of a [[ship]] when she is [[afloat]]; any of a series of short lines marked on the hull to show where the waterline would be under different [[loading]]s.
# {{lb|en|aviation}} A horizontal line indicating the shape of an airfoil.
# A line showing where the water has been, usually a line separating dry land and wet areas; a [[watermark]] or [[tidemark]].
# {{lb|en|cosmetics}} The inner rim of the eyelid, just behind the [[lash line]]; primarily used in reference to the application of [[eyeliner]].

